# NOTE: Assertions have been autogenerated by utils/update_mir_test_checks.py UTC_ARGS: --version 6
# RUN: llc -mtriple=amdgcn -mcpu=gfx950 -run-pass=machine-scheduler -o - %s | FileCheck -check-prefixes=CHECK %s
# RUN: llc -mtriple=amdgcn -mcpu=gfx950 -run-pass=machine-scheduler -amdgpu-release-credit-clusters=false -o - %s | FileCheck -check-prefixes=NOCLUSTER %s

# Regression test for the MFMA "released-cluster" tie-break in
# GCNMaxOccupancySchedStrategy::tryCandidate. The region below is the DS_READ /
# MFMA GEMM slice taken from a ck_tile FMHA kernel. The DS_READ loads form
# clusters of two; each cluster feeds one "pass 1" MFMA (uses %1) and one
# "pass 2" MFMA (uses %2), and the pass 2 MFMA accumulates onto the pass 1 result.
#
# During bottom-up scheduling, picking the pass 1 MFMA whose source load is the
# last outstanding member of a DS_READ cluster releases that whole cluster as a
# pack, so it must be preferred over a pass 2 MFMA that only frees isolated
# work. Concretely, the pass 1 MFMA consuming the offset-4672 load (cluster
# {4672, 4704}) must be scheduled after the pass 2 MFMA consuming the
# offset-4192 load, i.e. deferred to just before the final pass 2 MFMA.

--- |
  define amdgpu_kernel void @mfma_pass_cluster_release() { ret void }
...
